Once upon a time, there was a lighthouse keeper named Elias who lived on a remote island. Every night, he would stand at the lighthouse and wait for a boat to come. The boat was supposed to come every night, bringing him news and supplies from the mainland. But one day, the boat never came. Elias waited and waited, but no boat appeared. The days turned into weeks, and the weeks into months. Elias became more and more desperate, wondering if the boat had been lost at sea or if it had never come at all. Eventually, Elias gave up and stopped waiting. He knew the boat was never coming, and he had to accept that. The lighthouse stood alone on the island, a reminder of the boat that had never come.
