To remove a red wine stain from a cotton shirt, follow these steps:  1. Blot the stain with a clean cloth or paper towel to absorb as much of the wine as possible. Avoid rubbing, as this can spread the stain. 2. Rinse the area with cold water to remove any remaining wine residue. 3. Apply a small amount of dish soap or a stain remover to the stain. Gently rub it in with a soft brush or cloth. 4. Rinse again with cold water to remove the soap and stain. 5. Wash the shirt in the washing machine using cold water and a mild detergent. Check the care label for any specific instructions. 6. If the stain persists, you may need to repeat the process or try a different stain remover.  If the stain is still visible after washing, consider taking the shirt to a professional dry cleaner.
